WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:47.152
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:47.422 --> 00:48.173
That's enough, Bok!

3
00:53.470 --> 00:54.554
Sianong!

4
00:55.764 --> 00:56.598
Sianong!

5
00:57.640 --> 00:59.642
It's not too late for Chiara.

6
01:01.102 --> 01:04.189
Chiara isn't the one who's responsible for all of this.

7
01:04.272 --> 01:05.857
It's Vicky.

8
01:06.357 --> 01:08.401
You two go to Italy!

9
01:08.485 --> 01:09.486
I'm tired.

10
01:11.071 --> 01:11.905
Bok!

11
01:11.988 --> 01:12.947
Sianong!

12
01:13.031 --> 01:14.991
Sianong!

13
01:25.168 --> 01:28.421
I wish he had given us a chance to help him.

14
01:28.505 --> 01:31.424
But that doesn't justify betraying us.

15
01:31.508 --> 01:33.009
He was also a victim of a system

16
01:33.092 --> 01:34.886
that made him believe he had no other choice.

17
01:34.969 --> 01:36.888
We need to bring down the system

18
01:36.971 --> 01:38.473
that creates people like him.

19
01:39.891 --> 01:40.892
And the Concordat.

20
01:44.729 --> 01:46.523
-Definitely Italy. -Italy?

21
01:47.941 --> 01:49.734
So, what are you going to do in Italy?

22
01:49.818 --> 01:51.653
I have some friends there too.

23
01:53.404 --> 01:54.906
The Castellanis.

24
01:54.989 --> 01:57.242
One day, I'll take you there.

25
01:57.325 --> 01:58.368
Now I know why in Italy.

26
01:58.451 --> 02:00.453
-Why? -Sianong has friends there.

27
02:01.830 --> 02:02.747
Castellani?

28
02:02.831 --> 02:05.333
If that's Sianong's last clue to us,

29
02:05.416 --> 02:08.086
those are the people he wants us to find.

30
02:09.754 --> 02:10.839
Mom.

31
02:11.840 --> 02:13.508
Want to go shopping?

32
02:17.095 --> 02:18.555
My in-law texted.

33
02:19.931 --> 02:20.974
Tess.

34
02:21.057 --> 02:22.225
It's like

35
02:23.184 --> 02:24.727
she's sensing something

36
02:25.603 --> 02:26.688
about what happened.

37
02:27.397 --> 02:29.315
About what happened between you and Mikoy.

38
02:30.900 --> 02:32.068
What did she say?

39
02:47.959 --> 02:48.877
You know that?

40
02:53.172 --> 02:54.007
You're right.

41
02:56.843 --> 02:58.344
So what did you reply?

42
02:58.428 --> 02:59.387
What?

43
03:00.013 --> 03:01.055
I just hearted it, Chiara,

44
03:01.139 --> 03:03.600
because I didn't know what to say.

45
03:03.683 --> 03:05.935
I might say the wrong thing. Better not.

46
03:37.592 --> 03:38.468
Mama Yaya.

47
03:39.052 --> 03:39.969
Rahmboy.

48
03:40.845 --> 03:41.679
Chiara.

49
03:48.228 --> 03:49.229
Sianong…

50
03:49.312 --> 03:50.355
He's gone.

51
03:52.857 --> 03:54.567
He was careless.

52
03:54.651 --> 03:56.903
That's how the agency caught him.

53
03:57.487 --> 03:58.446
They chased him,

54
03:59.948 --> 04:01.991
and while he was trying to escape,

55
04:02.575 --> 04:03.493
he got into an accident.

56
04:07.997 --> 04:10.333
Human life is so fragile

57
04:10.416 --> 04:12.168
in this world of ours.

58
04:12.252 --> 04:13.544
Haven't you gotten used to it?

59
04:17.840 --> 04:19.008
I'm used to it.

60
04:21.803 --> 04:24.013
Well, is this going to be a problem?

61
04:24.681 --> 04:25.723
No.

62
04:26.683 --> 04:29.018
He can't talk now, so there won't be.

63
04:30.061 --> 04:32.563
Honestly, I thought about it too.

64
04:33.231 --> 04:35.316
It's better that Sianong is gone

65
04:35.400 --> 04:39.737
because I know he was the one who hated Mikoy the most.

66
04:39.821 --> 04:41.322
Now that he's gone,

67
04:41.406 --> 04:43.074
Mikoy is safer.

68
04:44.117 --> 04:45.493
Isn't that what you wanted?

69
04:49.080 --> 04:50.164
How is he?

70
04:51.624 --> 04:52.709
Mikoy?

71
04:53.751 --> 04:54.585
He's still alive.

72
05:07.181 --> 05:09.892
he has no way of getting to you anymore.

73
05:11.644 --> 05:13.563
That's probably for the best.

74
05:13.646 --> 05:15.398
With everything that's happening,

75
05:16.607 --> 05:19.652
he may be moving on too.

76
05:57.982 --> 06:01.235
the Castellani family was first known for their jewelry.

77
06:05.698 --> 06:07.450
their family business was at risk.

78
06:08.242 --> 06:10.787
And eventually, they slowly integrated themselves into the mafia world,

79
06:10.870 --> 06:11.746
just to survive.

80
06:12.455 --> 06:14.082
And it seems like it all paid off

81
06:14.165 --> 06:18.169
because currently, the new generation of Castellanis

82
06:18.252 --> 06:21.130
is the biggest threat to the Concordat's leadership.

83
06:21.631 --> 06:24.717
Well, aside from looking like models,

84
06:24.801 --> 06:27.845
the Castellanis certainly have a strong presence.

85
06:30.264 --> 06:32.016
Appeal isn't all they have.

86
06:43.611 --> 06:46.280
the Castellanis are currently negotiating with Chiara.

87
06:51.911 --> 06:54.413
Mom, Chiara, I'll go ahead.

88
06:54.497 --> 06:55.373
Okay, dear.

89
06:58.251 --> 06:59.335
Jeez.

90
06:59.418 --> 07:02.130
They rejected our counteroffer again.

91
07:02.964 --> 07:04.173
Yes, Chiara.

92
07:04.257 --> 07:05.633
They still won't agree.

93
07:05.716 --> 07:07.093
They're so conniving.

94
07:10.388 --> 07:12.473
Why don't they want to come to an agreement?

95
07:12.557 --> 07:14.684
What do they really want?

96
07:15.518 --> 07:18.479
Your position, of course, dear.

97
07:19.480 --> 07:22.567
Before you took over, what the Castellanis wanted

98
07:22.650 --> 07:26.863
was to lead and control the Concordat.

99
07:26.946 --> 07:28.656
But that didn't happen.

100
07:29.365 --> 07:31.117
So they're extremely bitter about it.

101
07:33.411 --> 07:34.745
So they're causing trouble

102
07:34.829 --> 07:38.291
just because they can't accept that I'm now the leader of the Concordat?

103
07:44.130 --> 07:47.258
Guys are indeed hard to understand.

104
07:47.341 --> 07:48.676
So stressful.

105
07:56.058 --> 07:59.645
So they're not fans of Chiara's leadership?

106
08:00.229 --> 08:04.358
I think it's not just because the Castellanis have appeal or influence.

107
08:13.576 --> 08:14.702
You're right, Dara.

108
08:15.244 --> 08:17.580
In fact, that's the trend these days.

109
09:21.769 --> 09:22.728
Can I use the phone?

110
09:23.271 --> 09:24.105
Sure, sir.

111
09:24.188 --> 09:25.815
No one's really using it anymore.

112
09:25.898 --> 09:27.608
Everyone just chats now.

113
09:27.692 --> 09:28.818
Thanks.

114
09:45.501 --> 09:46.419
I know they are in Italy.

115
09:46.502 --> 09:49.046
But Italy is too big, and I don't have enough time.

116
09:49.130 --> 09:51.299
If I have to know something as soon as possible,

117
09:51.382 --> 09:52.300
then tell me now.

118
10:13.029 --> 10:13.946
What's this?

119
10:14.614 --> 10:16.073
You're making a move on your own?

120
10:17.450 --> 10:18.909
And who were you talking to?

121
10:19.785 --> 10:21.120
My asset.

122
10:22.913 --> 10:23.748
Wow.

123
10:23.831 --> 10:25.291
And since when did you have an asset?

124
10:25.875 --> 10:27.627
That's not important anymore, Alex.

125
10:27.710 --> 10:28.794
What do you mean, it's not?

126
10:29.462 --> 10:30.796
Are you sure about this?

127
10:31.339 --> 10:32.298
And who is this person?

128
10:32.882 --> 10:34.258
They might get you into trouble.

129
10:34.342 --> 10:36.844
Just leave me alone, Alex. I know what I'm doing.

130
10:40.056 --> 10:41.182
Just let me have this one.

131
10:41.849 --> 10:43.684
It's safer if you don't know who they are.

132
10:43.768 --> 10:45.770
What matters is I can reach him through the landline,

133
10:45.853 --> 10:47.563
and he gives me vital information.

134
11:01.911 --> 11:02.745
‎Oh.

135
11:03.454 --> 11:04.288
What's the problem?

136
11:04.372 --> 11:05.873
-What happened? -What happened?

137
11:05.956 --> 11:07.792
What happened? Why?

138
11:14.590 --> 11:16.050
What did they say?

139
11:20.930 --> 11:22.890
they want to meet me.

140
11:27.728 --> 11:30.147
Finally, they're willing to talk.

141
11:31.065 --> 11:31.982
What's so good about it?

142
11:32.066 --> 11:33.526
What if they have a different agenda?

143
11:33.609 --> 11:34.985
What if-- What if they suddenly…

144
11:35.069 --> 11:36.612
Ambush! What if they ambush us?

145
11:36.695 --> 11:38.447
It's dangerous, dear. Don't do it!

146
11:38.531 --> 11:39.740
You're being dramatic.

147
11:39.824 --> 11:42.993
You're being way too negative. It's just a meeting, dear.

148
11:43.077 --> 11:45.830
Dear, you know I never lie to you.

149
11:45.913 --> 11:48.249
You know those Castellanis, they are cunning.

150
11:49.500 --> 11:51.419
We're going to prepare.

151
11:52.336 --> 11:54.547
They're cunning? That's their reputation.

152
11:54.630 --> 11:55.923
We won't back out.

153
12:32.418 --> 12:34.170
Italy is huge.

154
12:34.253 --> 12:35.421
Where in Italy?

155
12:37.923 --> 12:39.925
But are you sure Chiara Valtrovi will go?

156
12:42.595 --> 12:43.512
Yes, Mikoy.

157
12:43.596 --> 12:45.848
Isn't it dangerous for Chiara

158
12:45.931 --> 12:48.142
to meet with the Castellanis?

159
12:59.320 --> 13:00.154
Rahmboy, dear.

160
13:00.237 --> 13:02.490
You go with Chiara,

161
13:02.573 --> 13:06.911
so the Castellanis can see that we're training

162
13:06.994 --> 13:10.748
new generation of mafia leaders just like them.

163
13:37.775 --> 13:40.903
That's why the Moravianos don't take you seriously,

164
13:41.862 --> 13:43.697
if you're going to be this cowardly, Viktor!

165
13:58.796 --> 14:01.632
I'm the one who thinks things through.

166
14:01.715 --> 14:04.885
Between the two of us, I'm the one who takes action.

167
14:08.764 --> 14:10.182
You're so funny, you know that?

168
14:10.683 --> 14:14.186
You have no right to take action or make decisions.

169
14:19.441 --> 14:21.986
You're just sticking your nose in all this.

170
14:23.028 --> 14:24.655
Oh, I'm just sticking my nose in?

171
14:25.698 --> 14:28.909
You rich and powerful people,

172
14:29.493 --> 14:33.038
you think you have this huge illusion

173
14:33.122 --> 14:35.583
that you're the ones who make everything happen.

174
14:35.666 --> 14:38.502
But if it weren't for us poor people

175
14:38.586 --> 14:40.546
doing the work for you,

176
14:40.629 --> 14:41.797
you'd have nothing!

177
14:45.593 --> 14:49.179
We're just wasting time because you two keep arguing.

178
14:54.560 --> 14:56.103
Rahmboy, you're coming with me.

179
15:20.836 --> 15:24.423
Are you telling me, Mikoy, that you're getting all of this

180
15:24.506 --> 15:26.342
from your secret asset?

181
15:29.053 --> 15:30.179
There you go again.

182
15:32.973 --> 15:36.518
How can you say that your intel is legit?

183
15:36.602 --> 15:39.730
We don't even know who your asset is.

184
15:41.982 --> 15:43.192
You have a point, sir.

185
15:43.275 --> 15:46.654
We just got a little excited about the information he has.

186
15:48.572 --> 15:50.658
I'm skeptical too, just like you.

187
15:55.996 --> 15:57.206
See? You get it now?

188
16:00.709 --> 16:04.338
Even though Chiara is now the leader of the Concordat,

189
16:04.421 --> 16:09.343
she wouldn't risk her life or the lives of her people

190
16:09.426 --> 16:11.720
to meet with a group

191
16:11.804 --> 16:15.182
that clearly doesn't want her leading them.

192
16:16.809 --> 16:18.394
With all due respect, sir,

193
16:19.144 --> 16:20.896
you don't know Chiara.

194
16:21.772 --> 16:22.940
You don't understand her.

195
16:32.700 --> 16:33.784
Dear.

196
16:37.287 --> 16:39.081
Do not go, please.

197
16:39.665 --> 16:40.541
Remember,

198
16:46.296 --> 16:47.172
He's right, dear.

199
16:48.173 --> 16:49.425
Listen to your father.

200
16:54.930 --> 16:56.557
Whatever happened between Chiara and me,

201
16:57.141 --> 16:58.600
we still have a history.

202
16:59.184 --> 17:00.978
And that's my advantage over all of you.

203
17:02.271 --> 17:04.356
I'm sorry my asset is top secret.

204
17:05.065 --> 17:07.234
Maybe in time, you'll understand why.

205
17:10.237 --> 17:11.071
She's different.

206
17:12.239 --> 17:15.117
She wants every move she makes to make a statement.

207
17:19.163 --> 17:21.540
Especially now that she's the leader of the Concordat.

208
17:21.623 --> 17:24.043
She needs to prove through her actions

209
17:39.183 --> 17:40.642
But things are different now.

210
17:47.107 --> 17:49.568
What would they think of me?

211
17:53.072 --> 17:55.699
but the other Concordat groups as well.

212
17:55.783 --> 17:57.826
I'm sure all of them are waiting

213
18:15.344 --> 18:16.595
you're saying that

214
18:16.678 --> 18:19.431
Chiara is really going to Italy?

215
18:19.515 --> 18:21.266
I have a strong feeling she is, sir.

216
18:29.650 --> 18:30.818
Well, if that's the case,

217
18:31.819 --> 18:33.946
then all we have to do is wait for Chiara Valtrovi

218
18:34.029 --> 18:35.364
when she goes to Italy.

219
18:35.447 --> 18:36.573
Exactly!

220
18:37.407 --> 18:39.326
This is our golden window.

221
18:45.791 --> 18:49.211
How can we make sure Chiara will cooperate with us?

222
18:50.796 --> 18:51.630
Exactly, Mikoy.

223
18:51.713 --> 18:53.132
What if Chiara refuses to cooperate?

224
18:53.757 --> 18:55.217
Or refuses to be caught.

225
18:55.884 --> 18:56.718
What?

226
18:56.802 --> 18:58.470
You'll be playing cat and mouse in Italy.

227
18:58.554 --> 19:01.056
Or worse, it'll be catch me if you can all over Europe.

228
19:02.808 --> 19:03.892
Impossible.

229
19:03.976 --> 19:05.769
We don't have the budget for that.

230
19:08.438 --> 19:09.606
Back in Hong Kong,

231
19:10.190 --> 19:11.483
even though you tried to escape from us,

232
19:11.567 --> 19:14.027
you still cooperated with us even while the two of you were together.

233
19:14.736 --> 19:16.363
You had an agreement, and eventually,

234
19:18.282 --> 19:20.576
you ended up with very important information

235
19:20.659 --> 19:22.119
in exchange for a day.

236
19:26.790 --> 19:28.083
she won't back down.

237
19:34.965 --> 19:38.343
She managed to escape our law enforcement agency here.

238
19:39.636 --> 19:41.346
And it seems impossible

239
19:41.430 --> 19:44.349
that we can persuade her to come back to our country.

240
19:46.977 --> 19:49.438
Who came up with the idea of going to Italy

241
19:49.521 --> 19:51.607
to shake hands with criminals?

242
19:51.690 --> 19:52.691
Mikoy.

243
19:52.774 --> 19:56.028
Didn't we agree that we're there to get Chiara Valtrovi?

244
20:36.318 --> 20:37.194
Ouch!

245
20:41.406 --> 20:42.407
Are you okay?

246
20:44.243 --> 20:45.994
Me? Of course, I'm more than okay.

247
20:46.745 --> 20:49.289
I may endure some body pains,

248
20:49.915 --> 20:52.417
but at least I've got plenty of tricks up my sleeve.

249
20:52.501 --> 20:54.127
Right? Thanks to you.

250
21:01.176 --> 21:02.844
That's the spirit.

251
21:02.928 --> 21:05.180
That's the fighting spirit I want to see.

252
21:07.975 --> 21:09.977
But tell me something, Rahmboy.

253
21:12.729 --> 21:14.648
Can I trust you?

254
21:15.607 --> 21:16.566
Trust?

255
21:17.067 --> 21:17.985
Me?

256
21:18.068 --> 21:19.278
Of course!

257
21:21.488 --> 21:23.240
You really doubt me now?

258
21:25.325 --> 21:27.202
I heard that

259
21:27.286 --> 21:28.745
you've been having second thoughts.

260
21:29.288 --> 21:30.580
That you're not fully committed.

261
21:31.081 --> 21:31.915
Is that true?

262
21:33.417 --> 21:34.584
Chiara.

263
21:35.544 --> 21:37.004
I'm fully committed.

264
21:38.255 --> 21:41.049
There are probably still things I need to learn, but…

265
21:42.301 --> 21:43.135
I'm ready.

266
21:43.927 --> 21:44.928
And remember this.

267
21:48.015 --> 21:49.308
We're on the same side.

268
21:50.767 --> 21:52.311
You can count on me, Chiara.

269
22:01.028 --> 22:02.738
But I want you to remember this too.

270
22:04.281 --> 22:05.532
I'm on your side.

271
22:07.409 --> 22:10.620
If you have any doubts, it's better to tell me.

272
22:11.121 --> 22:13.248
Because from now on,

273
22:14.541 --> 22:16.460
you're my responsibility.

274
22:21.673 --> 22:22.507
Okay.

275
23:04.466 --> 23:08.178
But my gut feel tells me that this isn't an ordinary mission.

276
23:08.261 --> 23:09.971
We're going to a place

277
23:10.055 --> 23:14.142
where the most powerful mafia are gathering for a meeting.

278
23:14.226 --> 23:16.103
One mistake there,

279
23:16.186 --> 23:17.187
and we're all dead.

280
23:20.440 --> 23:23.401
In the mafia life, there's always one problem after another.

281
23:23.485 --> 23:24.611
Look at me.

282
23:24.694 --> 23:28.073
La Morte Bianca raised me and trained me.

283
23:28.156 --> 23:28.990
But…

284
23:29.074 --> 23:31.034
I still managed to stand against her.

285
23:31.118 --> 23:35.372
For now, let's focus on the Castellanis.

286
23:35.455 --> 23:39.167
We know how cunning they are. So let's be careful.

287
23:42.170 --> 23:43.839
You've been staring into space for a while now.

288
23:43.922 --> 23:45.924
I was just thinking about your brother.

289
23:46.007 --> 23:49.136
But you know, no matter how heavy the burden is,

290
23:49.219 --> 23:51.721
I'm sure he'll get through all of it.

291
23:51.805 --> 23:55.642
Why don't we show him that we're here, that we support him?

292
23:56.434 --> 23:57.352
I have an idea.

293
23:57.435 --> 23:58.895
Hello, Captain Pepe.

294
23:58.979 --> 24:01.314
I was hoping to ask you a favor.
